        "number": 8,
        "internalPageId": 8,
        "title": "When we talk about common life events we can use simple present and certain time phrases to state them in the future. Check the following examples.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "When we talk about common life events we can use simple present and certain time phrases to state them in the future. Check the following examples.",
          "TO CONSIDER 1. Use the simple present plus phrases in future to state them ahead in time. 2. The phrases must reflect a close future. 3. Respect the simple present rules.",
          "Simple Present + Future Phrase I have a test this Tuesday. Do you have a test this Tuesday? They have to do laundry this weekend. Do they have to do laundry this weekend? He goes for his school performance tonight. Does he go for his school performance tonight?"
        ],
